      <h1 id="migrating-from-jenkins-to-openshift-pipelines_{context}" class="group scroll-mt-20">Migrating from Jenkins to OpenShift Pipelines or Tekton<a href="#migrating-from-jenkins-to-openshift-pipelines_{context}" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p>You can migrate your CI/CD workflows from Jenkins to <a href="https://docs.openshift.com/pipelines/latest/about/understanding-openshift-pipelines.html">Red Hat OpenShift Pipelines</a>, a cloud-native CI/CD experience based on the Tekton project.</p>
      <h2 id="jt-comparison-of-jenkins-and-openshift-pipelines-concepts_migrating-from-jenkins-to-openshift-pipelines" class="group scroll-mt-20">Comparison of Jenkins and OpenShift Pipelines concepts<a href="#jt-comparison-of-jenkins-and-openshift-pipelines-concepts_migrating-from-jenkins-to-openshift-pipelines" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>You can review and compare the following equivalent terms used in Jenkins and OpenShift Pipelines.</p>
      <h3 id="_jenkins_terminology" class="group scroll-mt-20">Jenkins terminology<a href="#_jenkins_terminology" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h3>
